.UPDATE...
Issued at 915 AM PDT Tue Sep 1 2026

The deepening trough off of the Pacific Northwest and northern
California coasts is resulting in a mixing out of the marine layer
and temperatures as much as 20 degrees cooler than seasonal
averages. As such, ceilings have been around 3000 ft or greater much
of the night and into early this morning. Expecting these low clouds
to mix out and bring mostly sunny skies this afternoon. The
exception will be over the North Bay where high level clouds will
persist through much of the day. So updates are anticipated at this
time as the ongoing forecast remains on track.

