.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1039 PM PDT Mon Aug 31 2026
(Tonight through Wednesday)

Cool and wet. A deep 500 mb trough will slowly move towards the
coast over the next 24 hours. The marine layer is currently 3,200
ft deep as measured by the 00Z OAK sounding. This deep marine
layer, combined with the approaching trough, will very likely
bring some coastal drizzle Tuesday morning. Afternoon
temperatures will be 5-15 degrees below normal as the 850 mb
temperature drops below 10C/50F for the first time since May. By
Tuesday night a very weak cold front will bring a good chance for
light rain to the North Bay. This front will move southward
through the night and into Wednesday morning, bringing lower rain
chances to the rest of the Bay Area and Central Coast. Wednesday
will be similar to Tuesday with cool temperatures and another
chance for rain in the North Bay overnight as a second disturbance
moves through.

